      "title": "Info Edge Q2 billings rise 12.8% to ₹822 crore, recruitment segment grows",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/companies/news/info-edge-q2-billings-rise-12-8-to-822-crore-recruitment-segment-grows-126100800521_1.html",
      "description": "Info Edge (India) Ltd on Thursday reported a 12.8 per cent year-on-year increase in its standalone billings to Rs 822.3 crore for the second quarter ended September 30, 2026.\nThe company, which operates platforms, including Naukri.com and 99acres, had posted standalone billings of Rs 729 crore in the July-September period of the previous fiscal year, according to a regulatory filing.\nFor the first half of the financial year (H1 FY27), total standalone billings grew 13.5 per cent to Rs 1,559.3 crore compared to Rs 1,373.2 crore recorded in the corresponding period of the previous year.\nBillings from the recruitment solutions segment rose 12.6 per cent to Rs 613.8 crore during the second quarter, up from Rs 545 crore in the year-ago period.\n\"Adjusting for renewal timing differences, management estimates underlying growth in Q2FY27 at approximately 14-15 per cent YoY, against reported growth of 12.6 per cent,\" the filing said.\nThe real estate vertical, 99acres, recorded a 21.2 per ce",
